1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:03,800
[This series contains scenes of violence,
self-harm, and potential triggers.]

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:03,880
Hello.

3
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:05,120
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:05,180
Hello.

5
00:00:06,290 --> 00:00:07,490
What's your name?

6
00:00:08,170 --> 00:00:09,790
Lee Soohyun.

7
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:12,420
[Resume
Name: Lee Soohyun]

8
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:15,260
[Staff: Lee Doyoon]

9
00:00:15,990 --> 00:00:16,730
Doyoon,

10
00:00:16,770 --> 00:00:18,220
watch the register for me.

11
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:19,150
Coming!

12
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,000
May I take your order?

13
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,830
An iced Americano, please.

14
00:00:25,070 --> 00:00:25,810
Okay.

15
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:29,720
That's 4,700 won.

16
00:01:01,490 --> 00:01:05,670
[Lee Doyoon, Yoon Seojin,
Lee Wonwoo, Lee Chaeha...]

17
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:11,680
Please show me your ID.

18
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:19,140
[ID Card: Lee Hanyul]

19
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:19,789
Okay.

20
00:01:19,970 --> 00:01:21,030
That's 10,000 won.

21
00:01:22,380 --> 00:01:23,760
-Thank you.
-Goodbye.

22
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:27,770
[Cheongun-ru Restaurant]

23
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:31,110
Chaeha.

24
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:32,590
Yes?

25
00:01:37,130 --> 00:01:38,509
Your ID card.

26
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:40,509
-Ah...
-"Ah."

27
00:01:40,530 --> 00:01:41,840
-Right.
-"Right."

28
00:01:41,979 --> 00:01:43,640
Gosh, you forgot it again?

29
00:01:43,759 --> 00:01:45,509
I knew this would happen.

30
00:01:46,190 --> 00:01:48,070
I lost my ID card

31
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:49,970
and haven't had time to get a new one.

32
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:52,050
What are you so busy with all day?

33
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,860
Go apply for a new ID tomorrow.

34
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:54,940
You can come to work late.

35
00:01:54,940 --> 00:01:55,960
Got it?

36
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:58,360
Boss.

37
00:01:58,590 --> 00:02:00,950
I don't need
the employee insurance benefits.

38
00:02:00,950 --> 00:02:02,480
Can't I just work without it?

39
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,570
What?

40
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:05,470
Don't tell me you are...

41
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:08,860
a credit delinquent?

42
00:02:08,990 --> 00:02:11,020
Of course not.

43
00:02:11,150 --> 00:02:12,100
Then...

44
00:02:12,270 --> 00:02:13,840
an illegal immigrant?

45
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:14,950
No.

46
00:02:15,070 --> 00:02:15,970
-Right?
-Yeah.

47
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:17,480
Our restaurant follows the rules.

48
00:02:17,480 --> 00:02:18,910
I register all my employees.

49
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:20,370
Make sure to bring your ID by next week.

50
00:02:20,370 --> 00:02:21,400
Got it?

51
00:02:22,030 --> 00:02:22,950
Yes.

52
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:31,810
[Some scenes were created with AI.]

53
00:02:34,090 --> 00:02:37,820
[Adapted from the webtoon
"The Sound of Sugar Cubes" by Kim Tak]

54
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:40,630
[Screenwriter: So-on (JD)]

55
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:43,520
[Director: Yoon Jinyoung]

56
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,420
[Yoo Dohyun]

57
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:03,230
[Cho Chanhyeon]

58
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:04,860
[Ko Gyeol]

59
00:03:06,550 --> 00:03:09,780
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]

60
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,550
[Cheongun-ru Restaurant]

61
00:04:05,110 --> 00:04:07,210
Hello, this is Cheongun-ru.

62
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:15,170
Looks like I need to
find a new part-time job.

63
00:04:15,270 --> 00:04:17,940
Oh, yes. Your order is on its way.

64
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:20,410
Sorry?

65
00:04:21,870 --> 00:04:24,130
You want it delivered inside your house?

66
00:04:24,290 --> 00:04:25,440
Oh, okay.

67
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:26,640
Okay, got it.

68
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:29,010
Yes, your food will be there shortly.

69
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:32,659
Delivered inside the house? Weird.

70
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:34,600
Chaeha.

71
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,760
This delivery is for
Block A, Unit 102, right?

72
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:37,630
Yes.

73
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:39,360
They asked to have it delivered inside.

74
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:40,500
Inside the house.

75
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:42,670
Okay, got it.

76
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:37,690
Yes, Boss.

77
00:05:38,370 --> 00:05:39,510
It's been handled.

78
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:42,320
Understood.

79
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:53,760
Everything is ready.

80
00:05:55,110 --> 00:05:56,210
Please come in.

81
00:06:10,190 --> 00:06:11,420
Delivery.

82
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:18,620
Delivery!

83
00:06:23,150 --> 00:06:24,840
They asked to have it delivered inside.

84
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:26,020
Inside the house.

85
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:28,480
Inside the house.

86
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:03,070
Oh?

87
00:07:05,850 --> 00:07:07,220
Delivery.

88
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:11,100
Was that you singing just now?

89
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:13,330
Pay for your food.

90
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:16,860
Your singing still sucks.

91
00:07:18,650 --> 00:07:20,650
Don't tell me you want to be a singer.

92
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,580
Just pay for your food.

93
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:28,310
Wait here.

94
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:36,900
He really likes making people wait.

95
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:08,990
Look at this punk.

96
00:08:17,250 --> 00:08:18,850
Hello, this is Cheongun-ru.

97
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:21,470
I just ordered delivery
to Block A, Unit 102.

98
00:08:21,470 --> 00:08:23,610
Oh, um, has it not arrived yet?

99
00:08:24,010 --> 00:08:24,960
It has, but

100
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:27,690
the delivery guy stole my money.

101
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:29,900
Huh? Chaeha did that?

102
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:32,970
Oh, gosh, um, I'm so sorry.

103
00:08:34,270 --> 00:08:35,429
Chaeha...

104
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:37,900
Is his name Chaeha?

105
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:40,429
Yes. When he comes back,
I'll teach him a good lesson.

106
00:08:40,429 --> 00:08:42,909
I'll get him to apologize
and return the money to you.

107
00:08:42,909 --> 00:08:43,970
No, just fire him.

108
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:44,780
Sorry?

109
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:47,010
This employee seems problematic.

110
00:08:47,140 --> 00:08:48,580
Are you going to keep him?

111
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:50,670
Oh, of course not.

112
00:08:50,950 --> 00:08:52,720
You don't need to return the money.

113
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:54,340
Oh, okay. Sorr...

114
00:08:56,070 --> 00:08:58,210
Son of a... Rude bastard.

115
00:08:58,550 --> 00:08:59,860
Damn it.

116
00:09:15,510 --> 00:09:16,700
Chaeha.

117
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:21,630
So I couldn't find you all this time
because of your name.

118
00:09:27,350 --> 00:09:28,850
I'm back.

119
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:30,300
Lee Chaeha!

120
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:31,840
Did you steal from the customer's wallet?

121
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:32,620
Huh?

122
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,140
The customer just called

123
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:36,100
saying you stole from his wallet!

124
00:09:37,650 --> 00:09:39,070
I just took the money for the food,

125
00:09:39,070 --> 00:09:40,660
since he looked busy with work.

126
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:42,100
You dummy!

127
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:47,320
Today is your last day. Don't come back!

128
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:50,270
I only have myself to blame
for hiring someone without an ID.

129
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:51,900
I'm the idiot.

130
00:10:04,220 --> 00:10:08,200
Since you stole the money,
we're even for this month's wages.

131
00:10:08,330 --> 00:10:09,590
What do you mean steal?

132
00:10:14,310 --> 00:10:17,260
[High-paying part-time job:
Massage Therapist]

133
00:10:22,610 --> 00:10:23,900
[High-paying part-time job:
Massage Therapist]

134
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:31,200
[High-paying part-time job:
Massage Therapist]

135
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:46,410
I see. 173cm, 58kg?

136
00:10:46,530 --> 00:10:47,770
Nice.

137
00:10:48,130 --> 00:10:49,710
See you later.

138
00:11:01,490 --> 00:11:02,630
Massage?

139
00:11:07,950 --> 00:11:10,080
Are you the one I talked to on the phone?

140
00:11:13,590 --> 00:11:14,800
I...

141
00:11:15,430 --> 00:11:16,650
I don't think I can do this.

142
00:11:16,650 --> 00:11:18,190
Please leave...

143
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:22,330
You're quite hot.

144
00:11:50,170 --> 00:11:51,720
You were so hard to find.

145
00:11:52,050 --> 00:11:53,150
Hello.

146
00:11:54,230 --> 00:11:55,220
You...

147
00:11:55,450 --> 00:11:56,770
Are you crazy?

148
00:11:56,910 --> 00:11:58,560
Why did you choke him?

149
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:01,370
He isn't dead.

150
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:03,270
I just choked him out.

151
00:12:05,740 --> 00:12:07,530
I need to talk to you.

152
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:11,180
I couldn't let him take you away.

153
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:14,690
I'm good at giving massages too.

154
00:12:16,260 --> 00:12:17,480
Just kidding.

155
00:12:19,410 --> 00:12:20,940
You should try out for this.

156
00:12:22,660 --> 00:12:24,570
[Super Singer Audition]

157
00:12:27,370 --> 00:12:28,610
Why should I?

158
00:12:30,650 --> 00:12:32,330
If you don't,

159
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:35,960
I'll report you to the police
for stealing.

160
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,220
Hey, I didn't steal...

161
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:40,270
Oh, and the side of pickled radish
wasn't delivered.

162
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:42,180
That's a crime too.

163
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:45,400
The crime of missing radish.

164
00:12:46,170 --> 00:12:47,520
Get lost.

165
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:50,970
I signed you up with your real name.

166
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:55,180
Since your real name is pretty.

167
00:12:56,050 --> 00:13:00,380
[Super Singer Open Audition: Lee Hanyul]

168
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:06,520
You...

169
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,490
Who are you?

170
00:13:09,110 --> 00:13:10,150
Me?

171
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:12,930
Someone who makes music.

172
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:14,810
My name is Lee Won.

173
00:13:18,070 --> 00:13:20,870
Can I become a songwriter like Lee Won?

174
00:13:24,060 --> 00:13:25,970
1 PM at my place tomorrow.

175
00:13:26,290 --> 00:13:27,890
You know the address, right?

176
00:13:30,720 --> 00:13:33,780
You're running around incognito.

177
00:13:34,330 --> 00:13:36,590
There's no need to
make an enemy out of me,

178
00:13:37,330 --> 00:13:38,990
Mr. Missing Radish Criminal.

179
00:14:02,660 --> 00:14:04,110
That jerk...

180
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:05,790
is Lee Won?

181
00:14:09,770 --> 00:14:12,070
It's good, right? Super good, right?

182
00:14:13,650 --> 00:14:15,140
Don't force it on me.

183
00:14:16,150 --> 00:14:18,180
This is the songwriter Lee Won's new song.

184
00:14:18,180 --> 00:14:19,550
That Lee Won again?

185
00:14:19,890 --> 00:14:22,430
Sorry? "That Lee Won"? The disrespect.

186
00:14:22,430 --> 00:14:23,850
Is he your friend?

187
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:25,890
Funny you should mention that.

188
00:14:25,890 --> 00:14:28,290
Is he your friend?
I'm the one who's your friend.

189
00:14:27,990 --> 00:14:30,540
[Adolf] [Lee Hanyul]

190
00:14:28,890 --> 00:14:29,940
Forget it.

191
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:34,680
Hey, are you jealous?

192
00:14:35,070 --> 00:14:36,510
Why'd I be jealous?

193
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:37,990
You are jealous!

194
00:14:38,130 --> 00:14:39,420
I'm not!

195
00:14:40,630 --> 00:14:42,150
Don't be jealous.

196
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:45,790
I'll love him from afar forever.

197
00:14:46,860 --> 00:14:47,780
Tsk.

198
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:12,770
Here.

199
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:14,730
The radish you didn't get last time.

200
00:15:14,730 --> 00:15:17,920
Make sure you drink
every last drop of the brine.

201
00:15:20,690 --> 00:15:22,400
And this is the money I took.

202
00:15:22,780 --> 00:15:23,790
As for

203
00:15:23,950 --> 00:15:25,050
the audition,

204
00:15:25,620 --> 00:15:26,960
I'm not participating.

205
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:33,890
Y-route's leader Herod

206
00:15:34,030 --> 00:15:37,160
has gained immense popularity
with his aloof charm.

207
00:15:37,290 --> 00:15:39,790
Herod, please say hello to our audience.

208
00:15:40,550 --> 00:15:41,810
Hello, everyone.

209
00:15:42,340 --> 00:15:43,310
I'm Herod.

210
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:46,940
You're unveiling your title track
"Sound of Dawn" today.

211
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:51,040
I heard you actually wrote the lyrics
and composed the music yourself.

212
00:15:51,930 --> 00:15:53,070
Yes.

213
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:54,970
That's impressive.

214
00:15:55,110 --> 00:15:58,630
Herod, could you give us a little preview?

215
00:16:00,890 --> 00:16:03,010
The sound of dawn,

216
00:16:03,180 --> 00:16:06,740
my breath calling out to you.

217
00:16:07,310 --> 00:16:14,160
It may fade into the distance,
yet it still reaches toward you.

218
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:16,980
The sound of dawn,

219
00:16:17,130 --> 00:16:20,310
amid the stars that have
quietly fallen into slumber.

220
00:16:20,590 --> 00:16:24,580
Even as it softly echoes,

221
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:28,410
I am still here, waiting for you.

222
00:16:31,030 --> 00:16:32,330
How is it?

223
00:16:32,870 --> 00:16:33,970
It's good.

224
00:16:34,010 --> 00:16:36,370
It's way better than
what that Lee Won wrote.

225
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:37,370
Really?

226
00:16:37,570 --> 00:16:40,430
I wrote it with your voice in mind.

227
00:16:40,690 --> 00:16:41,840
Really?

228
00:16:42,260 --> 00:16:45,520
Was it you singing just now?

229
00:16:48,230 --> 00:16:49,740
Was it your voice?

230
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,010
Who are you?

231
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:53,960
The idol Herod.

232
00:16:56,470 --> 00:16:57,750
Sing it again.

233
00:16:59,250 --> 00:17:00,420
Why should I?

234
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,550
Because I want to hear it.

235
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:06,440
Who do you think you are?

236
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:13,109
Hanyul's voice sure is in great demand.

237
00:17:13,430 --> 00:17:15,089
Do you want to join our agency?

238
00:17:15,349 --> 00:17:16,810
Wow. Really?

239
00:17:17,010 --> 00:17:18,390
I'm not interested.

240
00:17:19,109 --> 00:17:21,640
Hey, why are you saying things
you don't mean?

241
00:17:22,230 --> 00:17:25,359
Our agency is going to hold
a Super Singer audition soon.

242
00:17:25,839 --> 00:17:27,609
I'll put in a good word for you.

243
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:28,770
Come try out.

244
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:32,480
Your number.

245
00:17:37,690 --> 00:17:39,140
What are you doing?

246
00:17:40,090 --> 00:17:41,370
This is my number.

247
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:43,270
Save it.

248
00:17:50,170 --> 00:17:52,540
Hanyul, are you going to debut?

249
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:55,960
Oh, please. He just asked me
to join an audition.

250
00:17:57,150 --> 00:17:59,410
He said he'd put in a good word for you!

251
00:18:02,670 --> 00:18:04,100
Do you know how many people

252
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:05,770
audition for such a big agency?

253
00:18:05,770 --> 00:18:09,030
But he gave you his number.
That must mean something.

254
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,850
Hey, do you want to audition too?

255
00:18:12,090 --> 00:18:13,520
M-Me?

256
00:18:13,660 --> 00:18:15,280
Yeah, let's do it together.

257
00:18:15,750 --> 00:18:17,920
He didn't mention me at all.

258
00:18:18,060 --> 00:18:21,140
That's because he hasn't heard you sing.

259
00:18:21,790 --> 00:18:23,660
No need. Forget it.

260
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:27,050
You're mad, aren't you?

261
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:28,280
I'm not mad.

262
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:30,040
You're mad he didn't ask you.

263
00:18:30,050 --> 00:18:31,230
I said I'm not mad.

264
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:32,430
You're so mad.

265
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:34,310
I said I'm not mad! You really...

266
00:18:34,310 --> 00:18:36,100
You turd!

267
00:18:40,650 --> 00:18:41,840
Lee Hanyul!

268
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:44,210
Lee Hanyul!

269
00:18:45,230 --> 00:18:46,410
Lee Hanyul!

270
00:18:47,750 --> 00:18:49,880
Lee Hanyul, let's go to the music room!

271
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:59,340
Hey, where's Lee Hanyul?

272
00:19:00,230 --> 00:19:02,820
He just left with Adolf, I think.

273
00:19:21,400 --> 00:19:23,440
The position of your hand
should be like this.

274
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:24,580
Lee Hanyul.

275
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:26,450
Oh, you're here.

276
00:19:26,650 --> 00:19:27,660
Herod.

277
00:19:30,450 --> 00:19:32,540
What are you two doing?

278
00:19:34,140 --> 00:19:37,310
He's pestering me,
saying he wants to try composing too.

279
00:19:37,320 --> 00:19:39,180
Isn't it just pressing some keys?

280
00:19:39,540 --> 00:19:40,770
Hey.

281
00:19:41,370 --> 00:19:44,120
Your hand position is wrong to begin with.

282
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:47,240
Like this with your left hand

283
00:19:47,950 --> 00:19:49,090
and like this

284
00:19:49,290 --> 00:19:50,400
with your right.

285
00:19:54,340 --> 00:19:55,570
Oh, right, Herod,

286
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:57,750
your agency's audition you mentioned,

287
00:19:57,750 --> 00:19:59,350
can Adolf try out too?

288
00:20:00,030 --> 00:20:01,020
Don't.

289
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:02,600
Why?

290
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:04,200
Please, Herod,

291
00:20:04,220 --> 00:20:05,900
you can make it happen, right?

292
00:20:05,930 --> 00:20:07,260
Please do us this favor.

293
00:20:07,270 --> 00:20:08,370
He can really sing.

294
00:20:08,490 --> 00:20:09,640
Give him a chance.

295
00:20:11,400 --> 00:20:12,270
Okay.

296
00:20:12,500 --> 00:20:13,880
-Really?
-Really?

297
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:16,820
I can't thank you enough.

298
00:20:17,530 --> 00:20:19,930
No, I should be thanking you.

299
00:20:20,650 --> 00:20:22,430
By the way, your song at the audition...

300
00:20:22,430 --> 00:20:23,070
Yeah,

301
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:24,030
I've decided.

302
00:20:24,290 --> 00:20:25,260
Which song?

303
00:20:25,900 --> 00:20:27,240
Sound of Dawn.

304
00:20:28,110 --> 00:20:30,800
But no one knows this song.

305
00:20:30,950 --> 00:20:32,810
Didn't you say you wrote it for me?

306
00:20:32,990 --> 00:20:35,160
It's the only song like it in the world.

307
00:20:35,170 --> 00:20:37,070
A song made just for my voice.

308
00:20:39,440 --> 00:20:42,130
Wow, Sound of Dawn.

309
00:20:42,250 --> 00:20:44,170
Herod, absolutely no one can

310
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:45,970
pull off this song but you.

311
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:47,250
Really?

312
00:20:48,890 --> 00:20:50,970
What do you want from me?

313
00:20:51,420 --> 00:20:52,650
I told you

314
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:55,260
I want you to join
the Super Singer audition,

315
00:20:55,750 --> 00:20:58,840
Lee Hanyul.

316
00:21:00,420 --> 00:21:02,410
If you make it to the finals,

317
00:21:02,880 --> 00:21:04,680
I'll help you get that song back.

318
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:09,890
How about it?

319
00:21:10,490 --> 00:21:13,550
This is your only chance to
get your friend's song back.

320
00:21:16,270 --> 00:21:17,870
This time...

321
00:21:24,470 --> 00:21:25,840
If you still...

322
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:30,910
Go to hell, you bastard!

323
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:32,840
This is unbelievable.

324
00:21:32,910 --> 00:21:33,910
Are you filming?

325
00:21:36,540 --> 00:21:38,070
Do nothing...

326
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:41,000
It was so cringe watching him

327
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,950
show off on the piano in the music room,
pretending to be a composer.

328
00:21:43,950 --> 00:21:45,690
It's boring to end it like this.

329
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,660
Would a guy's hole be tighter?

330
00:21:48,310 --> 00:21:51,240
He's a goody-two-shoes model student,
so I bet it is.

331
00:21:55,270 --> 00:21:57,200
Are you planning to run away again?

332
00:22:21,650 --> 00:22:24,950
[The Sound of Sugar Cubes]
